course: dictionary
lesson: 14987
title: Repose, a word for calm rest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Repose is a formal word. You will meet it in old poems, classic stories and church prayers, and rarely in everyday talk. Context helps you work it out.
explain: «The old cat lay by the fire in perfect repose.» The cat is not running, playing or hunting. It is resting quietly, so repose means calm rest. Test it: if "calm rest" fits the sentence, you have found the meaning.
explain: Repose can also be a verb, meaning to lie down or rest. «The tired king reposed on his soft bed.» Look for clue words like "tired" and "bed" to see that the king is resting.
fact: Repose is a noun meaning rest, sleep or calm.
fact: As a verb, repose means to lie down or rest, or to be placed somewhere.
fact: «Repose» is an old-fashioned, formal word found in poetry and classic books.
fact: «A face in repose» means a face that is calm and still.
fact: In science, the angle of repose is the steepest slope a pile of sand or gravel can have before it slides.
exercise: «The baby slept in peaceful repose.» What does repose mean here? | Loud noise | Running fast | A bowl of soup | *Calm rest
exercise: Ravi learned that the angle of repose is the steepest slope sand can keep before it slides. What is it? | *The steepest slope a pile of sand can have before it slides | A kind of sandcastle | A measure of how heavy sand is | The name of a sandy beach
exercise: «The tired dog decided to repose on the rug.» Which words mean the same as repose here? | *Lie down and rest | Cook a meal | Shout loudly | Run around the garden
test: «Grandma sat in the garden in quiet repose, her eyes closed.» What does repose mean? | *Calm rest | Angry shouting | Noisy hurry | Fast running
test: Christians pray for the repose of the souls of the dead. What does repose mean in "the repose of the soul"? | A loud party | Sadness and tears | A busy day at work | *The peaceful rest of someone who has died
exam: Which word could replace repose in «The sleepy baby was in deep repose»? | Shopping | *Sleep | Hurry | Noise
